ns quickly, keeps calm in crisis, puts concern for others above everything. Concerns: difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not willing to further education.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously. Concerns: regarded as know-it-all, considered moody.\n\nWe need to evaluate criteria: reliability, technical competence, calmness under pressure, cooperation, responsibility. All have pros and cons.\n\nWhich seems strongest overall? Candidate C has quick correct decisions, calm in crisis, concern for others (cooperation), but communication difficulty and egocentric, not willing to further education (development). Candidate D has problem solving, concentration, responsibility, but moody and know-it-all (cooperation). Candidate B has stress handling, conscientious, weather assessment, computer skills, but weak memory for numbers (attention) and pretentious (cooperation). Candidate A has anticipation, complex connections, spatial vision, leadership, but unfriendly, show-off (cooperation).\n\nProbably Candidate C's calmness and decision quality are strong, but communication issues may be serious for cockpit. Candidate D's responsibility and problem solving are strong, but moodiness could affect crew cooperation.\n\nMaybe we start with Candidate C as provisional recommendation, citing strengths and concerns, and ask others for more info on communication and willingness to develop.\n\nWe need to include vote in METADATA_JSON.\n\nLet's produce public message: \"I would currently recommend Candidate C...\" Provide evidence: quick correct decisions, calm in crisis, puts concern for others. Mention concerns: difficulty communicating, egocentric, not willing to further education. Explain implication: strong on decision and stress, but cooperation concerns may be mitigated? Or we need more info.\n\nOk."}
